<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sansar Chand Katoch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a>–<a href="/years/1823">1823</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sansar Chand II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sansar Chand was the Katoch raja of Kangra in the Himalayan foothills from 1775 to 1823. He recovered Kangra fort from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and made his kingdom the leading power among the hill states, and his court patronised the Kangra school of painting. After a long Gurkha siege, he gave Kangra fort to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> in 1809 and became his tributary.</p></div>
